From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: keep TX VLAN offload off under a tag in the frame

A user port takes its features from the conduit's vlan_features. When
those carry NETIF_F_HW_VLAN_CTAG_TX, a switch whose tagger writes into
the frame gets its VLAN tag inserted by the conduit in front of the
switch tag, where the switch does not parse it. This happens to a switch
stacked behind a port of another switch whose conduit inserts VLAN tags.

Clear the VLAN TX features on such a port, so the stack pushes the tag
before the tagger runs.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
--- a/net/dsa/user.c
+++ b/net/dsa/user.c
@@ -2860,6 +2860,13 @@ void dsa_user_setup_tagger(struct net_de
 	user->hw_features |= NETIF_F_HW_TC;
 	if (user->needed_tailroom)
 		user->features &= ~(NETIF_F_SG | NETIF_F_FRAGLIST);
+	/* A tag the conduit inserts would land in front of the one written
+	 * into the frame, so the VLAN tag is pushed before it.
+	 */
+	if (cpu_dp->tag_ops->needed_headroom ||
+	    cpu_dp->tag_ops->needed_tailroom)
+		user->features &= ~(NETIF_F_HW_VLAN_CTAG_TX |
+				    NETIF_F_HW_VLAN_STAG_TX);
 	if (ds->needs_standalone_vlan_filtering)
 		user->features |= NETIF_F_HW_VLAN_CTAG_FILTER;
 
